    \end{align}
    where we use the fact that $y^*\in P_s(G)$ is binary.  

    Now, let $d$ be a feasible direction at $(x^*,y^*)$, such that $d=(\bar{x},\bar{y}) - (x^*,y^*)$ for some $(\bar{x},\bar{y})\in\Delta_n\times P'_s(G)$. We can separately consider $d=(d_x,d_y)=(\bar{x}-x^*,\bar{y}-y^*)$, where $d_x$ and $d_y$ are feasible directions for the $x$ and $y$ components of the optimization problem at $x^*$ and $y^*$, respectively. 
Furthermore, for any $U\subseteq V$, we denote by $d_U:=(d_x)_U$ the restriction of the $x$-component of $d$ to the coordinates indexed by $U$.



    Then we can compute
    \begin{align}\@bsphack
